 "integrity": "Inference inputs: our eval tracks (store run 20261025-evperc-4f596df, library_v3-seeded, tier P1), eval FoundationStereo depth, E0 eval hands (MediaPipe), calibration, the kit mesh_budget, the public t0_C0b and the C0b public picks / candidates (frame check). No scan, mocap, parquet pose, *_align file or library mesh was an input to any build or choice (e0b_stage.py asserted the upload); library_v3 / C0 / E0 meshes were read only in the reported-only stage after the pick. Nothing was tuned on eval; E0b is not scored (no eval ground truth).",
 "not_a_drop_in": "library_e0b / library_e0bx are library_v3 / library_v3x with only the adopted objects replaced. Pack 9a+ ships C0 pot / lid / rack, the C1 beige lathe and the C1 dust pan: packing either folder whole reverts those pairs. Merge the adopted objects one by one into the pack library.",
 "caveats": [
  "IN-SAMPLE PICK: obs_fidelity on the same eval points the candidates were fitted to; the C0b public pick is out-of-sample there (the 0.85 margin of rule 9 (e) is the only allowance). Fidelity is not CD-O.",
  "CUBE-ROI CLUTTER: the 0.30 m cube admits static clutter (public C0b: 3 of 5 objects failed for this reason); fidelity on cluttered points can reward meshes that explain the clutter.",
  "MARKER BALLS: the frozen gmg detector found mostly implausible ball counts on public dev files (B7) and on the C0b public picks (pot 26, rack 45); the eval picks carry the counts given in objects.<o>.e0b_pick.n_balls.",
  "POSE BOARDS: the packed mesh also drives AUC / MPPE / RPE / SR; the C0b AUC guard ran on the public picks, not on these eval-built meshes."
 ]
